course: dictionary
lesson: 14866
title: Reactivate: make it work again
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: The prefix re- means again, and active means working or switched on. So reactivate means to make something work again, or become active again, after it has stopped. «Please reactivate your account to log in.» The account had stopped working, and now it works again.
explain: You can also reactivate things that are not computers. «The guard reactivated the alarm after the repair.» The alarm had been switched off, and now it is switched on again. Ask yourself: was it stopped before? If yes, reactivate probably fits.
explain: In science, reactivate means to start a chemical, a volcano, a virus or a process working again. «Scientists fear the sleeping volcano may reactivate.» Check your meaning by swapping in "start working again" and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: The prefix re- at the start of a word often means again, so reactivate means active again.
fact: «Reactivate» means to make something work or become active again after it was stopped or switched off.
fact: «Reactivate» can also mean to start a chemical, a volcano, a virus or a process working again.
fact: The chickenpox virus can stay quiet in the body for years, then reactivate later as shingles.
fact: Useful phrases: «reactivate an account», «reactivate the alarm», «reactivated volcano».
exercise: «I forgot my password, so I need to reactivate my account.» What does reactivate mean here? | Delete the account for ever | *Make the account work again | Write a new password on paper
exercise: «The guard reactivated the alarm after lunch.» What had happened to the alarm before? | *It had been switched off | It had been moved to the garden | It had been painted blue
exercise: Scientists think the sleeping volcano may reactivate. What could happen? | It will be painted by artists | *It may start working again and erupt | It will stay asleep for ever | It will turn into a lake
test: What does the re- at the start of reactivate mean? | Very big | Not | Under | *Again
test: «The chickenpox virus can reactivate years later as shingles.» What can reactivate years later? | *The chickenpox virus | The shingles rash | The school nurse | The sunny weather
exam: «Maya wants to reactivate the old game on her tablet.» Which phrase means the same as reactivate? | *Start working again | Delete | Give to a friend | Hide from view
